WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.897
Episode two: the folders, and the main loop.

2
00:00:02.897 --> 00:00:06.057
If you only watch one episode, make it this one.

3
00:00:06.407 --> 00:00:08.730
Every folder answers one question.

4
00:00:08.730 --> 00:00:11.052
Fields: how is one question drawn?

5
00:00:11.052 --> 00:00:13.989
Sections: how is a block of the page drawn?

6
00:00:13.989 --> 00:00:16.107
Actions: what does a button do?

7
00:00:16.107 --> 00:00:18.020
Evaluators: is an answer OK?

8
00:00:18.020 --> 00:00:21.845
And offline: how does it keep working without a network?

9
00:00:22.195 --> 00:00:25.468
Here is every file, with what it does and how long it is.

10
00:00:25.468 --> 00:00:30.119
Most files are under seventy lines, so you can read any of them in a few minutes.

11
00:00:30.119 --> 00:00:32.129
BaseField is the one to read first.

12
00:00:32.481 --> 00:00:35.174
This table is built from the real import lines.

13
00:00:35.174 --> 00:00:39.357
Utils imports nothing, and fields know nothing about sections or buttons.

14
00:00:39.357 --> 00:00:42.336
That keeps every part easy to understand on its own.

15
00:00:42.688 --> 00:00:43.782
Now the main loop.

16
00:00:43.782 --> 00:00:48.037
When a technician taps a button, the field calls setValue on the form.

17
00:00:48.037 --> 00:00:50.589
That is the only way a value ever changes.

18
00:00:50.940 --> 00:00:54.056
setValue stores the answer in one object, form.

19
00:00:54.056 --> 00:00:54.520
values.

20
00:00:54.520 --> 00:00:57.570
Then it calls refresh, which asks every field,

21
00:00:57.570 --> 00:01:01.415
and then every widget, to redraw itself from those values.

22
00:01:01.767 --> 00:01:02.359
That’s it.

23
00:01:02.359 --> 00:01:05.495
One place for data, and one way to update the screen.

24
00:01:05.495 --> 00:01:09.222
When something looks wrong, there is exactly one place to look.

25
00:01:09.574 --> 00:01:11.611
Here is refresh in the real code.

26
00:01:11.611 --> 00:01:14.760
Step one: calculated fields work out their numbers.

27
00:01:14.760 --> 00:01:17.415
Step two: every field updates its own look.

28
00:01:17.415 --> 00:01:21.551
Step three: every widget updates what it collects from many fields.

29
00:01:21.903 --> 00:01:23.952
You can see this for yourself.

30
00:01:23.952 --> 00:01:26.683
The sample page puts the form on window.

31
00:01:26.683 --> 00:01:27.571
formRenderer.

32
00:01:27.571 --> 00:01:30.439
In the browser console, type formRenderer.

33
00:01:30.439 --> 00:01:30.917
values.

34
00:01:31.268 --> 00:01:35.051
Calling setValue from the console does exactly what a tap does.

35
00:01:35.051 --> 00:01:37.212
Watch the first tab change its name.

36
00:01:37.563 --> 00:01:39.363
Next time: fields and rules.

37
00:01:39.363 --> 00:01:44.315
How one question is drawn, and how the form decides whether the answer is OK.
